# #419: File -> New Level, then "+" (a new world) in the new level. The menu, its item and the "+" next to the world tab
# are found by name (#1130, editor/ui_probe), so the run does not depend on the layout or the theme.
# The scene is clean at the start, so New Level asks nothing.
# The editor logs "Created a new level" and "Created world 'world2'" (tools/headless/check_log.sh reads them).
sleep 1
shot headless_out/new_level_world/00_start.png
click_item menu File
sleep 1
shot headless_out/new_level_world/01_file_menu.png
click_item menu New Level
sleep 4
shot headless_out/new_level_world/02_new_level.png
click_item hierarchy_tabs +
sleep 1
shot headless_out/new_level_world/03_plus_popup.png
type world2
key Return
sleep 4
shot headless_out/new_level_world/04_world2.png
